```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Dark Mode Toggle</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #f5f5f5;
      --text: #1a1a1a;
      --card: #ffffff;
      --button-bg: #1a1a1a;
      --button-text: #ffffff;
    }

    html.dark {
      --bg: #121212;
      --text: #e8e8e8;
      --card: #1e1e1e;
      --button-bg: #e8e8e8;
      --button-text: #121212;
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
      transition: background 0.3s ease, color 0.3s ease;
    }

    .card {
      background: var(--card);
      padding: 2rem 3rem;
      border-radius: 12px;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
      text-align: center;
      transition: background 0.3s ease;
    }

    button {
      margin-top: 1rem;
      padding: 0.6rem 1.4rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 8px;
      cursor: pointer;
      background: var(--button-bg);
      color: var(--button-text);
      transition: background 0.3s ease, color 0.3s ease, transform 0.1s ease;
    }

    button:hover { transform: scale(1.05); }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="card">
    <h1 id="label">Light Mode</h1>
    <button id="toggle">🌙 Switch to Dark</button>
  </div>

  <script>
    const html = document.documentElement;
    const button = document.getElementById("toggle");
    const label = document.getElementById("label");

    function applyTheme(dark) {
      html.classList.toggle("dark", dark);
      label.textContent = dark ? "Dark Mode" : "Light Mode";
      button.textContent = dark ? "☀️ Switch to Light" : "🌙 Switch to Dark";
    }

    // Restore saved preference, or fall back to the OS setting
    const saved = localStorage.getItem("theme");
    const prefersDark = window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches;
    applyTheme(saved ? saved === "dark" : prefersDark);

    button.addEventListener("click", () => {
      const dark = !html.classList.contains("dark");
      applyTheme(dark);
      localStorage.setItem("theme", dark ? "dark" : "light");
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

How it works:

- **CSS variables** hold the color palette for both themes; toggling the `dark` class on `<html>` swaps the values everywhere at once.
- **A button** flips the theme and updates its own label/icon.
- **Persistence**: the choice is saved to `localStorage`, so it survives page reloads. On first visit it respects the OS-level `prefers-color-scheme` setting.
- **Transitions** on `background` and `color` make the switch smooth instead of jarring.

Save it as `index.html` and open it in any browser — no dependencies needed.
